AltoStaking::deactivateContainer()
├── when caller is not owner
│   └── it should revert
└── when caller is owner
    ├── given container is not deprecated
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── given container does not exist
    │   └── it should revert
    └── given valid container exists and is deprecated
        ├── when container is active
        │   ├── it should deactivate container
        │   ├── it should emit ContainerDeactivated event
        │   └── when container is max multiplier container
        │       └── it should update max multiplier to next highest active container
        ├── when container is already inactive
        │   └── it should revert
        └── when multiple containers are deactivated
            └── it should deactivate all and update max multiplier to zero if none active
